00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.589 align:start position:0%
 
unless you've been living under a rock  you've probably tried asian skincare  products already skincare culture is a  bit different in asia so there are lots  of awesome asian products that we don't  really get in western countries plus  they're usually budget-friendly today  i'm going to be reviewing some really  awesome asian beauty products i've tried  recently as well as some that were  pretty bad a lot of these are products  that viewers have recommended to me  they're some of those cult asian  products that you've heard a lot about  online yes it is mostly sunscreens there  are five in there but there's also some  cleansing products as well as makeup  this video is sponsored by starvana  which is why i got all of these they  have a massive range of asian beauty  products they've also given us a  discount code to use as well we're  starting with the can make mermaid skin  gel uv this is an spf 50 plus pa 4  pluses sunscreen it was a holy grail  sunscreen of mine but then they  reformulated or repackaged i'm not  entirely sure so it looks like the old  version which i really loved became the  clear version and the whitening one that  one purposely makes your skin a little  bit whiter which is quite popular in  asia this sunscreen is really  beautifully light on the skin it's also  unscented and it's not really siliconey  i have this problem where when i use  sunscreens with a lot of silicones they  often become quite oily throughout the  day on my skin it also doesn't have  alcohol i know alcohol is a problem for  a lot of people it's not really an issue  for me but if that's what you're looking  for this is great it works really well  under makeup and there's zero white cast  on my skin at least it's also fine  around my eyes there's none of that eye  stinging now the filters in this there's  octanoxate juvenile a plus zinc oxide  titanium dioxide and tino sorbets i  reviewed the old version and this is the  same so this is back up to holy grail  status i highly recommend it our next  sunscreen is the neville uv super water  gel 50. this is spf 50 and pa with three  pluses so it's a little bit low in  protection than the can make sunscreen  this is a super lightweight sunscreen  and it has this effect where when you  put it on your skin it feels like it  bursts into water so it feels super  refreshing after you've applied it it is  very lightweight but you can still feel  it a little bit on your skin this is the  80 gram bottle if you buy the slightly  larger version it comes in a convenient  pump the filters are octanoxy dhhb and  octal trizone it does have a pretty  strong alcohol smell when you put it on  at first my main issue with it is the  slightly lower protection but as an  everyday sunscreen it is really nice now  onto two of the more confusing  sunscreens i've tried lately the isn't  tree sunscreens these are both from the  hyaluronic acid range and as you can  tell they look pretty much the same and  that's where the confusion came in that  both spf 50 plus and pa with four pluses  i saw julian scamander14 who does a lot  of sunscreen reviews on instagram he has  really dark skin and he was using one of  these and it looked fantastic on his  skin so i was really excited to try this  of course i grabbed the wrong one which  is the perfect sunblock  the packaging is really not friendly for  those of us who are usually in a rush  and not super observant the perfect  sunblock peeled massively on my skin and  i was actually rushing off to a picnic  with one of my friends who has brown  skin and i was going to give him a  sunscreen and i packed this one of  course and then i noticed it turning  white on my skin so then i had to pull  that out of the bag he didn't turn up to  the picnic anyway so i guess it was fine  i did end up using it on my arms which i  forgot to put sunscreen on before the  picnic so luckily i had this and it is  quite nice on the arms it uses titanium  dioxide which is why it has this  massively whitening effect some people  have asked me if a titanium dioxide only  sunscreen can actually have this pa plus  plus plus claim in other words can it  actually be broad spectrum and give good  uva protection the answer is yes a lot  of older books and papers say that  titanium dioxide can't give good uva  protection but there are newer titanium  dioxide ingredients out there now that  tick off the criteria for broad spectrum  on their own so they give a good spread  of uva and uvb protection titanium  dioxide is a particular mineral  sunscreen ingredient which means it is  in lots of little solid particles with  these solid particulate sunscreen  ingredients there are lots of things  that you can change like the particle  size and the surface treatments that  will change how that ingredient performs  when it goes under uv so in other words  what uv wavelengths it will absorb more  so for example kroda which is a cosmetic  ingredient company they give an example  formulation that uses their own titanium  dioxide ingredients and it ends up with  spf 65 and uva pf26 which would  translate to the same rating as this i  don't know the exact titanium dioxide  ingredient that this sunscreen is using  of course but  that rating is possible with just  titanium dioxide but anyway the white  cast and the pilling disqualified this  for me and overall it was just a very  rude experience but it turns out the one  that i was meant to get was the watery  sun gel and this one is a really nice  sunscreen it uses a whole bunch of  organic sunscreen ingredients so  octophylate homozylate be mt mbbt  polysilicon 15 and dhhb it's pretty nice  and light and hydrating it's not as  ridiculously light as the neville or the  biore but it is really good for oily  skin it could probably stand to be a  little bit more hydrating though  sunscreen number five is the thank you  farmer sun project light sun essence  this is an spf 50 plus but only pa with  three pluses this applies with a similar  sort of silky feeling as the can make  sunscreen but it is a bit heavier it has  a whole bunch of chemical sunscreen  ingredients dhhv octanoxate octazylate  homozylate and octocrylene the fact it's  a bit heavier and the lower uva rating  means that this can't make it into my  holy grails but i think it is quite a  nice everyday sunscreen if you have  maybe drier skin and you want something  a little bit heavier that can double up  as moisturizer now on to the cleansing  products this is the unique calendula  complete cleansing oil this is a  fragrance free cleansing oil which  usually i'm a little bit hesitant about  but  it smells like a cooking oil and i can't  actually smell any rancidity in this  that's that slightly sour smell that you  sometimes smell in oils usually with  cooking oils when you've had them open  for too long i have only had this for a  few months but i also can't find any  reviews that have ever mentioned it so  it's quite possible that it stays  non-rancid for quite a while a lot of  cleansing oils have noticeable rancidity  after a few months and that's because a  lot of oils will oxidize with oxygen and  light if the oils in a cleansing hole  aren't selected carefully especially if  they're using plant oils and especially  if there's no masking fragrance then  this rancidity can be a bit of an issue  and it's much more obvious because this  is the sort of product that you would  put really close to your nose so this is  actually a really nicely done fragrance  free cleansing oil i would still prefer  something that didn't smell so much like  cooking oil but if you can't handle  fragrance and you prefer plantars in  your cleansing oils then this is a  really nice option you can also pick  ones which have more stable oil so you  would avoid any plantars that have lots  of linoleic acid for example maybe stick  to things like mineral oil jojoba oil  and squalane this is pretty good at  getting rid of makeup and it rinses off  pretty cleanly and it comes in my  favorite packaging for cleansing all  which is a pump bottle really convenient  the only thing is i do like a little bit  of a subtle fragrance in my cleansing  products and that's the same problem i  have with the harder labo gokujian  hydrating face wash this is a cleanser  that comes with a foaming top and it is  fragrance free which is a selling point  for a lot of people but it's just not  really up my alley this is a really nice  cleanser it's not very hydrating it's  not very stripping either and it is  pretty much just fine in every way but  it's just a little bit joyless i didn't  realize this would be such an issue for  me but  it just kind of felt like a chore to use  it feels a bit like the skincare version  of soylent nutritionally it's exactly  what you need with nothing extra but  kind of feels a bit flavourless i  definitely prefer it over a product  that's really nice to use but strips my  skin massively but i would just prefer  something a little bit more exciting but  for those of you who just want a really  solid cleanser that works well and has  no frills then this would be a fantastic  pick it just isn't really my cup of tea  now on to the makeup this is the hair  essential spicy nude balm in naked  almond that is a lot of innuendo for a  lipstick this is actually the lipstick i  am currently wearing i guess we don't  really talk about asian makeup a lot  because makeup is something that it's a  lot easier to try in person so this was  a bit of a blind buy but i'm really glad  i got it it is a really pretty brick red  color it looks a lot like my favorite  lipstick which is toast of new york by  revlon but it's a sheerer color and it  looks more like a gloss there is a  little bit of a minty feeling on my lips  not a ton  and the fragrance is really nice it  smells like a cup of tea i also really  prefer this sort of stick format which  is a little bit harder to find with  asian brands most asian brands that i've  looked at have those doe foot gloss like  applicators and while they're okay  they're not my preferred way of applying  lipstick i prefer a much more oily  product i think maybe i'm just not quite  coordinated enough to deal with a doe  foot on a daily basis i also tried some  gel eyeliners from the brand mercy  these gel eyeliners stay on really well  and they didn't transfer at all even  though my eyelids are super oily this  one is a normal sized one and this one  is a slim eyeliner both of these don't  blend that well once you've put them on  your skin you do have to work quite  quickly and so if you're using your  finger just like apply it smudge it  apply the next part smudge it again i am  wearing it on my eyelids at the moment  and you can see i haven't really  bothered blending it much because it is  actually quite difficult the regular  eyeliner comes with a sharpener in the  end that you can pull out  now the slim one is really cool it is  only 1.5 millimeters in diameter which  means it's really thin it's really easy  to control and you can draw a really  good cat eye with it really easily it  does tend to break off really easily  because it is so slim so the mercy  website does give a tip where you only  wind up so there's about a millimeter  sticking up before you start using it  the problem is because it is so skinny  there isn't that much product inside  this like the cylinder total mass is  just tiny it is 0.05 grams which is 50  milligrams versus  in the big one you have 10 times as much  of that solid black product 0.5 grams  and even that isn't very much product  compared to my usual revlon colorstay  cream gel which is 1.2 grams so it's a  bit more than twice as much as in the  big one and it is  24 times as much as in the slim one so  while the slim one is a really cool  product and i haven't really seen  anything like that on the market before  it is something to keep in mind it is  probably not going to be the product  that you use to draw a really thick  eyeliner line on every day so all of  those are from starvanna they've given  me a discount code which is right here  if you've tried any of these products  before let me know what you thought of  them please consider subscribing if  you've learned something new also click  the notification bell so you don't miss  any uploads and i will see you next time  to nerd out more

